*
*/**
# vsce already ignores **/.DS_Store, but a `!` pattern overrides every ignore
# regardless of order, so each re-include has to exclude it itself. The
# alternation is what makes that work: vsce appends a "/**" folder variant to
# any pattern whose last segment holds no "*", and that variant matches the
# very files the pattern just excluded. Putting a "*" in the last segment
# stops the variant from being created.
!node_modules/**/!(.DS_Store|*.DS_Store)
!dist/extension.js
!package.json
!README.md
!CHANGELOG.md
!LICENSE
!resources/**/!(.DS_Store|*.DS_Store)
!schema/**/*
